nate. (Ayes 71. Noes 0. Page 1664.)","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-05-23","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118225381","location":"Senate","sequence":12,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"In Senate. Read first time. To Com. on RLS. for assignment.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-committee","code":null,"date":"2025-06-04","eventType":"committee_action","historyId":"118225382","location":"Senate","sequence":13,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Referred to Com. on E. & C.A.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-committee","code":null,"date":"2025-07-15","eventType":"committee_action","historyId":"118225383","location":"Senate","sequence":14,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"From committee: Do pass and re-refer to Com. on APPR. with recommendation: To Consent Calendar. (Ayes 5. Noes 0.) (July 15). Re-referred to Com. on APPR.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-committee","code":null,"date":"2025-08-19","eventType":"committee_action","historyId":"118225384","location":"Senate","sequence":15,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"From committee: Be ordered to second reading file pursuant to Senate Rule 28.8 and ordered to Consent Calendar.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-08-20","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118225385","location":"Senate","sequence":16,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Read second time. Ordered to Consent Calendar.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-08-21","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118225386","location":"Senate","sequence":17,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"From Consent Calendar.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-08-21","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118225387","location":"Senate","sequence":17,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Ordered to third reading.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-09-03","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118225388","location":"Senate","sequence":18,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Ordered to inactive file at the request of Senator Valladares.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_AMENDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Section 15306 of the Elections Code is amended to read:"}],"approvedDate":null,"chapter":null,"chapteredDate":null,"committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"bf318b68caeb593d49aab67e1a706838e63c37b094c6ed5be78c0ac8ec4d00a1","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Existing law requires elections officials, beginning no later than the Thursday following an election, to post updated election results on their internet website at least once per week until publication of the certified statement of results or until the only ballots left to count are vote by mail ballots for which a voter has the opportunity either to verify or provide their signature.\n\nThis bill would increase that posting requirement to at least twice per week. By increasing the duties of local elections officials, this bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that, if the Commission on State Mandates determines that the bill contains costs mandated by the state, reimbursement for those costs shall be made pursuant to the statutory provisions noted above.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_enacted","date":null,"note":"Not enacted as of the date of the data (of